      "documentSlug": "pd-medication-timing-interactions-and-hospital-safety",
      "documentConcept": "PD medication timing, interactions and hospital safety",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:c7ade22f23946b8dac8571aca70f79c318fa7eb87f9fa31b814af94dcc1d3b17",
      "text": "Medication safety in Parkinson disease depends on preserving individualized dose times, avoiding abrupt interruption, planning administration during fasting or swallowing problems, and checking medicines that block dopamine or interact with the existing regimen. NICE and hospital safety resources emphasize appropriate timing, specialist involvement and accurate medication records. Pharmacy recommendations address reconciliation, custom order times, alerts, medicine availability and careful substitution. Protein redistribution requires nutritional safeguards. Antiemetic choice must account for drug-specific contraindications. Observational evidence about whether medication delays prolong hospital stay is conflicting, so hospital length-of-stay findings should not be presented as universal causal effects.",
      "sources": [
        "https://dailymed.nlm.nih.gov/dailymed/fda/fdaDrugXsl.cfm?setid=3235535d-9ef9-4657-8b2a-176a807d091c",
